# ==========================================================================================
# === EXECUTABLE-LIFT bridges — the SAME questions, asked of the LIFTER'S OWN OUTPUT ======
# ==========================================================================================
# Bridges Q1–Q6 above are answered by tests/fixtures/bridges.ttl, a HAND-AUTHORED scene
# under <http://example.org/math/>. The four questions below are their producer-namespace
# twins: each runs the analogous query over tests/fixtures/lifted-{r,onnx,proof}.ttl, which
# are byte-for-byte the output of gmeow_math::producers::{r_lift,onnx_lift,proof_lift} (the
# shipped gmeow_math_lift front-ends, run over real committed artifacts and pinned by
# crates/math/tests/lift_fixture_drift.rs). They close the producer-without-a-consumer gap:
# the bridge competency surface is now interrogated against what a parser actually derived,
# not only against what an author wrote down.
#
# Every expected IRI below was READ OUT of the committed fixture. The local names are
# content-addressed on the lifted bytes, so these rows are falsifiable in the strongest
# available sense: a lifter regression that changes what is derived changes the hash, and
# the cell reds without anyone having to notice.

# === Lifted Q1 — the R lift's source, fidelity rung, and logic: routing ==================
