    gmeow:cqRationale "Each piecewise function reports its pieces, the interval each governs, and the qualitative analytic behaviour (monotonicity kind or magnitude bound) each carries; over the fixture the answer is exactly the two pieces {leftPiece over leftInterval, strictly decreasing; rightPiece over rightInterval, bound 0.001}. The bound is projected as a string so a numeric literal shares one column; monotonicity and bound are LEFT-JOINed, so a piece carrying one but not the other still appears with its sub-domain." ;
