# === The two flagship signed-radial-field scenes ============================ #
# The qualitative scene: the whole target recovered with NO closed form. The seven
# rows are the two divergent poles, the plateau bound, and the four ring masses.
ex:cqRadialFieldQualitative a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/grounding/math/queries/competency/radial-field-qualitative.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqDataFile "examples/signed-radial-field-qualitative.ttl" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The qualitative flagship scene models a signed radial field on a compactified Lorentzian 2-plane WITHOUT any equation; the competency proves the whole story is recoverable as data. Over the scene the answer is exactly the seven rows: the central singularity limit → math:PositiveInfinity (R′), the infinity limit → math:NegativeInfinity, the Ring-2 plateau bound 0.01, and the four ring measure evaluations {μ(Ring 0)=0.1, μ(Ring 1)=0.25, μ(Ring 2)=0.55, μ(Ring 3)=0.1} — Ring 2 the strictly-dominant plateau band. Values are projected as strings so the pole IRIs, the bound, and the masses share one column." ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqRadialQualShape ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:rowRadialCentre , ex:rowRadialInfinity , ex:rowRadialPlateau ,
        ex:rowRadialRing0 , ex:rowRadialRing1 , ex:rowRadialRing2 , ex:rowRadialRing3 .

